{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Brings.BringConjugationChirality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Brings.BringConjugationChirality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.letterSign_ne_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.letterSign_ne_conj","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L162-L167","doc":"Under the matching, a configuration and its conjugate select opposite letters: so the\nselection is chiral exactly when the configuration is pinned to one side. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.ChiralityMatching.letterSign_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.ChiralityMatching.letterSign_conj","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L160-L160","doc":"The matching: conjugation is the bar involution on the selected letter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.ChiralityMatching.letterSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.ChiralityMatching.letterSign","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L158-L158","doc":"The crossing sign selected at the configuration (`true` = `σ`, `false` = `σ⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.ChiralityMatching.rot_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.ChiralityMatching.rot_conj","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L156-L156","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.ChiralityMatching.rot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.ChiralityMatching.rot","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L155-L155","doc":"The C₅ rotation exponent at the configuration's fixed point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.ChiralityMatching.conj_invol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.ChiralityMatching.conj_invol","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L153-L153","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.ChiralityMatching.conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.ChiralityMatching.conj","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L152-L152","doc":"The curve's conjugation acting on configurations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.ChiralityMatching.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.ChiralityMatching.mk","kind":"ctor","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L150-L150","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.ChiralityMatching","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.ChiralityMatching","kind":"class","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L145-L160","doc":"**Chirality matching.** Over an abstract set `X` of collision configurations with an\noriented-angle map, the curve's conjugation and the Hecke bar involution act compatibly:\nthe bar involution on the letter (`σ ↔ σ⁻¹`, encoded as `letterSign`) is the conjugation on\nthe configuration. With this, a configuration pinned to one member of a conjugate pair\nfixes a crossing sign. No instance: nothing in the corpus derives it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.ut_lift_preserves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.ut_lift_preserves","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L137-L141","doc":"The differential of `ι` on `UT(Σ)`, locally `(x, y, θ) ↦ (x, −y, −θ)`:\norientation-PRESERVING. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.sigmaI_lift_reverses","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.sigmaI_lift_reverses","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L132-L135","doc":"`ι × id` on `Σ × I`, locally `(x, y, t) ↦ (x, −y, t)`: orientation-REVERSING. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.even_unique_minimiser_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.even_unique_minimiser_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L121-L128","doc":"**An even energy with a unique minimiser on a symmetric interval selects `φ = 0`**:\nneither crossing sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.pairAverage_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.pairAverage_even","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L115-L119","doc":"**Conjugation-invariant energies average to an even function.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.pairAverage","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.pairAverage","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L111-L113","doc":"The energy at a point and at its conjugate, as functions of the oriented angle,\naveraged over the pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.rotExp_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.rotExp_injective","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L104-L107","doc":"**The four fixed points of one 5-cycle carry four distinct rotations.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.rotExp_ne_rotExp_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.rotExp_ne_rotExp_neg","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L98-L102","doc":"**No fixed point is chirally neutral**: its rotation differs from its conjugate's. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.rotExp_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.rotExp_neg","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L94-L96","doc":"**Conjugation reverses the rotation.** `p_{−j}` is the conjugate of `p_j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.rotExp_eq_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.rotExp_eq_neg","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L91-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.rotExp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.rotExp","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L87-L89","doc":"The rotation exponent of the 5-cycle at `p_j`: the tangent line `e_{2j}` against the\npoint `e_j`, i.e. `ζ^{j − 2j}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.residues_distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ConjugationChirality.residues_distinct","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringConjugationChirality.lean#L78-L85","doc":"The five Fourier residues at the fixed point `p_j` are pairwise distinct for `j ≠ 0`:\n`0`, `−j`, `−2j` (killed by the Jacobian), `j` (the point), `2j` (the tangent line). ","signatureChunk":0}]}